Subject: [PATCH RFC] wifi: mt76: add opt-in Airoha SDK-24 NPU RX for MT7915/MT7916

Add a separate receive transport for the legacy NPU protocol. Keep radio
TX and TX completion on the host and require an explicit firmware ABI,
model and PCIe topology. The transport is experimental, disabled by
default, and deliberately keeps all packets on the host during bring-up.
The old SDK-16 and the Wi-Fi 7 HW-RRO protocols are not interchangeable.

The legacy protocol has no documented DMA-drain acknowledgment: retain
published DMA storage until reboot and refuse recovery/restart after stop.
This is a hardware bring-up RFC, not production-ready NPU acceleration.
Requires the Airoha NPU startup/command-capability prerequisite patch.

diff --git a/mt7915/Kconfig b/mt7915/Kconfig
--- a/mt7915/Kconfig
+++ b/mt7915/Kconfig
@@ -23,3 +23,13 @@
 	  This adds support for the built-in WMAC on MT7981 and MT7986 SoC device
 	  which has the same feature set as a MT7915, but enables 6E
 	  support.
+
+config MT7915_NPU
+	bool "MT7915/MT7916 experimental Airoha NPU receive support"
+	depends on MT7915E
+	depends on NET_AIROHA_NPU=y || MT7915E=NET_AIROHA_NPU
+	help
+	  Enable the legacy Airoha NPU receive transport. This requires the
+	  SDK 24-byte receive ABI, a single PCIe DBDC radio, matching firmware,
+	  an explicit device-tree configuration and npu_enable=1.
+	  Transmit processing remains on the host. If unsure, say N.
